{
	"_about": "hazel: a 43.8s vector-construction launch film for a graphics or illustration model, derived frame-by-frame from a 43.8s launch film (1280x720 @25fps). Authored directly in reference px on the 1280x720 stage, rendered at device scale 1.5: render.mjs --fps 25 --scale 1.5. Placeholder product: Filbert 2.0 (a fictional vector-graphics model). Everything is drawn in code: pale line art stroking on, halftone marks, an easing curve on a sky field, a word drum, code over an illustration, letterforms and outlines built point by point, four-frame mockup and stamp montages, a prompt loop, and a wordmark close.",
	"_sections": "S1 0-7.52 sky pill, panel-wipe line, three split screens | S2 7.52-15.68 word drum with tiles, sky and easing curve | S3 15.68-23.24 code over illustration, letterforms, outline, frame strip | S4 23.24-28.60 mockup montage, table of work | S5 28.60-33.84 prompt, generation, stamps | S6 33.84-43.84 loader, two claims, wordmark",
	"_slots": "Image slots: `src` on any tile, mockup or stamp entry replaces the drawn stand-in (mockup items in s4-mockups, stamp items in s5-stamps, tiles in s1-live, s2-drum, s4-table, s6-claim, plus `src` on s1-split-camera and s3-code). Without a src, the drawn art renders.",
